1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,860
Things that quietly disappeared in American schools.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:05,360
Today's kids will never experience.

3
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,700
There's no book anymore with so many names written in it.

4
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:12,120
Kids today probably have never heard the sound of paper being cut.

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:17,160
Those old TV carts are obsolete now, and no kid is going to cheer for one anymore.

6
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:23,220
Back then, everyone looked forward to book fair day, some even too excited to sleep the night before.

7
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:26,720
Holographic notebooks were all the rage at school.

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:29,180
Do kids still play Heads Up 7-Up?

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,340
I used to choose my secret crush when I played.

10
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:37,340
The Boston Pencil Sharpener was top tier back then, only the teacher's desk had one.

11
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,060
We used to sneak over to the desk and try to peek at the report cards.

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:46,280
During lunch, we'd all pull out those plastic-smelling lunchboxes with our favorite characters on them.

13
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:50,400
This was the game we played in computer class, and now no one even remembers it.

14
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:56,320
We didn't have cell phones, so if we wanted to contact our families, we had to wait in line at the payphone.

15
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,280
If you remember these things, tell me how old you are.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,400
We'll see you then.

17
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,700
We'll see you then.

18
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:04,400
We'll see you then.

